Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 01:37:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] fix(readyz): report not ready when the database schema is
 behind this build

/readyz returned 200 "ready" with database "configured" for any reachable
database, including one still at migration 0004. Every procedure touching
tables from 0005-0010 (provider policies, OAuth login transactions, durable
tasks, MCP connectors, upload sessions) would then fail at request time.

Readiness now compares information_schema.COLUMNS for the connected database
against every table and column the Drizzle schema declares. A missing table
or column gives 503 with database "schema_mismatch"; extra objects are
allowed (forward-only additive migrations); a read failure is "unknown" and
not ready. The unauthenticated response carries counts only; the missing
table names go to the server log.

Reproduced on a built server against MySQL 8 at baseline 0004: before 200
ready, after 503 schema_mismatch (11 tables, 1 column missing); fully
migrated database: 200 ready, schema current.

Tests: unit (compare/expected/unknown), real-MySQL 0004-vs-current, and the
E2E readiness spec now asserts the schema is current.

